WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.207
Some cleaning shortcuts make a dataset look better while reducing its truthfulness.

00:00:05.207 --> 00:00:08.352
A bad date should not become today's date.

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:12.417
A negative price should not become positive without evidence.

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:17.937
A missing phone should remain missing unless a reliable source provides one.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:23.297
A possible duplicate should not be deleted just because its ID is larger.

00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:27.617
Cleaning should preserve uncertainty when the truth is unknown.

00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:33.357
Once a quality rule is well understood, prevention may be better than repeated cleanup.

00:00:33.357 --> 00:00:37.557
Constraints can stop known invalid values at write time.

00:00:37.557 --> 00:00:43.722
When updates are required, preview the target rows, change only what is justified,

00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:48.631
and use RETURNING or an audit log so the transformation can be reviewed.
